Z||000000||Monkeyman||10-19-2000||08:43 PM||||Because of a small monetary windfall, I'll probably get a new motor sooner than I expect.  Hopefully in the next couple of months.  I need to get the tranny rebuilt at the same time.  I figure that will cost about $500.  I won't have much more than 3 grand total to spend.  That leaves me with about $2500 to spend on a motor.<P>What are my choices?<P>I can get my current motor rebuilt (probably into a 3.2) for around 2 grand by a local mechanic.  Any V8 (N* or SBC) is way out of my price range as is a 3800.  That only leaves the 3.4.  I know that Ed Parks can install a good 3.4 and rebuild the tranny for around $3300, but I'd need to get the car to Alabama.  Too far and I just can't afford to be without my car for very long.  Anyone know about what Bob Steiger charges for the same?<P>The only other performance mod I hope to do at the same time is upgrade the exhaust.  I plan on keeping it fairly simple.  No cat or mufflers, only a set (4) of Supertrapps.<P>What options do I have with the money I have?  Remember that I'm mechanically challenged so I won't be doing any of the work myself.<P>Sort of thinking out loud, but if I go the cheapest route (rebuild by my local mechanic), I might actually have enough money left over for Mr. Mikes carpet and seat covers as well as some other small stuff I've been looking at.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||5
