Z||000010||batboy||10-21-2000||12:31 PM||||Sometimes it's cheaper to get a remanufactured short block than it is to rebuild your old engine. The downside is, they usually stick a stock cam in it, but some companies give you an option to change the cam for an extra fee. Then you could build the Fiero heads up real nice and still afford the headers and a cool exhaust system. Building a 3.1/3.2 out of a 2.8 is nice, but you should be able to have a nice running 2.8 with an extra 20+ ponies under the decklid, even if you don't stroke it. Remember, if you have a tired engine right now, just a fresh stock rebuild will seem great in a nimble little Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Monkeyman||10-21-2000||11:28 PM||||Reman short block from where?  Jasper is the only one I know of for sure, but I'm sure there are others.  Might be a good idea to check into that.<P>And how can I get an extra 20+ ponies under the decklid from the stock engine?  Going from my tired motor to a freshly rebuilt one with an extra few hp will feel like a V8 to me (at least for a while).  I could use the extra money for some other stuff.||||reg||1
